From 2d241eba281e32265286ceeef5a4f84a10e45051 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AxelGalvez11 <axelgalvez1121@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:53:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(nemesis): consent gate, bug-report button, plan-includes
 copy, student settings trim
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New NemesisConsentGate (student build): one-time plain-language privacy +
  responsibility screen after first sign-in. Truthfully names data processors
  (DeepSeek/Tavily/Firecrawl/Supabase), states what stays local (portal logins,
  recordings, files), read-only portals, and the check-your-syllabus line.
  Acceptance stored in localStorage keyed by consent version.
- Account dialog: 'Report a bug' button (prefilled mailto to
  support@enternemesis.com); stale beta copy pointing students at
  Settings->Providers replaced with plan-includes-Nemesis-intelligence copy
  (metered proxy is the product; no BYOK).
- STUDENT_SETTINGS_KEEP: drop 'providers' and 'config:model' — provider/key/
  model settings are not student-facing (de-vendor + business model).
- ALSO INCLUDES pre-existing uncommitted Codex WIP on nemesis-account-gate.tsx
  (trial countdown reminder, entitlement revalidation on focus/interval,
  device-key removal) — swept in because the file was edited in place; its
  test passes against this state.
- Verified: tsc/vite build clean; electron platform tests 311 pass / 0 fail;
  nemesis-account-gate.test.tsx 2/2. Note: broad vitest UI failures exist on
  this WIP branch from other uncommitted Codex work (stale-js masking);
  unrelated to this commit.
